&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Emplifi&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://emplifi.io/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Emplifi&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; is the only&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://emplifi.io/platform-overview/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt; Autonomous CX platform&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; unifying social marketing, commerce, and customer care for more than 20,000 brands worldwide. Powered by Fuel AI, built on more than 5T of data, and recognized as a leader by leading industry analysts, Emplifi helps enterprise teams orchestrate connected customer journeys and deliver personalized experiences at scale, turning every customer touchpoint into a competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Emplifi&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://emplifi.io/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Emplifi&lt;/a&gt; is the only &lt;a href=&quot;https://emplifi.io/platform-overview/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Autonomous CX platform&lt;/a&gt; unifying social marketing, commerce, and customer care for more than 20,000 brands worldwide. Powered by Fuel AI, built on more than 5T of data, and recognized as a leader by leading industry analysts, Emplifi helps enterprise teams orchestrate connected customer journeys and deliver personalized experiences at scale, turning every customer touchpoint into a competitive advantage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Product Team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Emplifi, our mission is to transform how digital marketing—especially on social—is done, and how consumers connect with brands in the 21st century.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product team sits at the heart of this mission. We build and evolve a data-driven SaaS platform that helps global enterprises market smarter. By bridging customer needs, business goals, and technical innovation, we break down silos, foster collaboration, and use insights to guide smart, impactful decisions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced, data-driven &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to shape the future of Emplifi’s Data Insights capabilities — a core product area that enables brands to understand conversations, uncover emerging topics, and act on market signals that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is about building intelligence that helps brands understand what people care about, how perceptions evolve, and where opportunities arise across digital channels. You’ll be leading a product area that helps marketers and strategists collect the right data and turn them into actionable insight—at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the roadmap, vision, and execution for this strategic capability, partnering closely with design, engineering, data science, and go-to-market teams to create powerful, intuitive experiences for enterprise users. This includes managing integrations with external data providers to ensure scalable, high-quality access to insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position is remote/hybrid from within the Czech Republic, the UK, France, or Germany.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In today’s world, tracking discourse, sentiment, and context across digital sources gives brands a competitive edge. Organizations that move fast to uncover trends, surface risks, and respond to emergent feedback win. You’ll lead a product at the intersection of data, AI, and strategy helping the world’s leading brands stay in tune with conversations, perceptions, and signals that shape their markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is passionate about turning complex, unstructured data into clear insight and action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands how enterprise marketers, analysts, and strategists use insights to guide decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can translate business challenges into scalable, data-driven solutions powered by AI and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a space where technology, storytelling, and customer empathy meet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do Here&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the vision and roadmap&lt;/strong&gt; for one of the Data Insights product line — setting direction based on customer needs, market dynamics, and company goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive product discovery&lt;/strong&gt; - talking to customers (brands and retailers), observing behavior, synthesizing data, and identifying unmet needs and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate ideas into execution&lt;/strong&gt; - write clear requirements, work with design and engineering, and iterate fast to deliver impactful, high-quality solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a market expert&lt;/strong&gt; - understand the competitive landscape and adjacent categories, monitor trends in ecommerce and AI, and translate them into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage data partnerships and integrations &lt;/strong&gt;- oversee connections with third-party data providers and APIs, ensuring consistent, reliable data access. Evaluate vendor performance, react quickly to API or data schema changes, and balance product impact against integration costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner cross-functionally&lt;/strong&gt; - collaborate with Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, and Leadership to position the product for success across the customer lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure what matters&lt;/strong&gt; - define success metrics, analyze outcomes, and refine based on learnings to ensure continuous improvement and customer value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Bring to Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years of experience in Product Management, &lt;/strong&gt;ideally in B2B SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track record of product impact&lt;/strong&gt; – You’ve successfully led products through key stages of their lifecycle, whether taking over complex existing solutions or driving new launches, and can demonstrate how you improved outcomes and measured results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep familiarity with AI in practice&lt;/strong&gt; — you actively use AI tools to enhance your workflow and have experience defining, delivering, and iterating on AI-powered features that create tangible value for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High autonomy &amp;amp; maturity&lt;/strong&gt; – You’re ready to own a product stream within your first 90 days, defining strategy, uncovering new problems, and driving delivery without hand-holding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global mindset&lt;/strong&gt; – Comfortable collaborating with colleagues and customers across time zones and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile mindset&lt;/strong&gt; – Experienced in iterative releases, and data-driven optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical fluency &amp;amp; AI awareness&lt;/strong&gt; – You can talk architecture with engineers, understand how complex distributed systems fit together, and spot opportunities to apply the latest AI/ML advances to solve customer problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent, persuasive communicator&lt;/strong&gt; – You write, present, and negotiate confidently in English while actively listening, distilling insights, persuading stakeholders, and selling product value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive problem-solver&lt;/strong&gt; – You spot issues, rally the right people, and deliver solutions. No waiting for task lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;BONUS POINTS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with managing products that rely on external or third-party data sources. Comfortable analyzing ROI, negotiating data costs, and adapting quickly to changes in API availability or pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with analytics, data visualization, or insight-generation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in social media, audience research, or digital strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for empowering organizations to make smarter, faster, data-driven decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We Offer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chance to work with the world’s biggest brands at the CX tech leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick Days &amp;amp; Community Service Days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multisport card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maternity and Parental Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile and open-minded culture, with high levels of trust and flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity for professional growth and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possibility to learn new and cutting-edge technologies, in an environment that encourages new ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-first workplace, with access to leading AI tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and more), empowering you to work smarter, innovate faster, and build AI skills for the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in an international environment in our modern offices in Karlín, with our big terrace and our own grill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There’s more as well! Speak with us to find out all the details!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Emplifi, we are committed to creating a workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to bring their whole selves to work. We welcome applications from individuals of all ages, races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, gender identities, and LGBTQ+ communities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Emplifi offers a safe, inclusive, and supportive environment where every employee has the opportunity to thrive and is encouraged to be who they are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We welcome and encourage applicants with disabilities. Accommodations are available upon request at any stage of the recruitment process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Emplifi, we are committed to creating a workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to bring their whole selves to work. We welcome applications from individuals of all ages, races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, gender identities, and LGBTQ+ communities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Emplifi offers a safe, inclusive, and supportive environment where every employee has the opportunity to thrive and is encouraged to be who they are.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;We welcome and encourage applicants with disabilities. Accommodations are available upon request at any stage of the recruitment process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Too Good To Go, we dream of a planet with no food waste.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Did you know that more than 40% of all food produced gets thrown away? This unnecessary food waste — and the resources needed to produce and transport it — accounts for 10% of global greenhouse gas emissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Too Good To Go is a certified B Corporation on a mission to end food waste. We connect stores with surplus food to consumers across 20 markets in Europe, North America, and APAC — with over 140 million registered users, more than 200,000 daily active stores, and 600 million meals saved from going to waste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pricing sits at the centre of everything we do. It shapes what partners earn, what consumers pay, and how much surplus food actually gets saved. Today, pricing decisions are made in different places, for different reasons, without a single team owning the strategy end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are changing that. We are building our first dedicated Pricing team — and you will be the founding member.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will start with a concrete, high-value problem: the pricing infrastructure behind our Key Account deals. That&#39;s your launchpad — from there, you will have real scope to shape our approach to dynamic pricing, consumer-facing service fees, and pricing strategy across Too Good To Go more broadly. This is a role built for someone who wants to define a domain, not just execute a brief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The goal behind everything we do is twofold: save as much surplus food as possible, and grow the pie between TGTG, our Partners, and our Consumers — never trading one off against the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is a further dimension to this. We are expanding beyond food into new non-food, non-perishable categories — and that growth brings pricing complexity and opportunity we have not had to solve before. Getting ahead of that, rather than reacting to it, is part of this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager for Pricing, you will build the foundation for how Too Good To Go prices its marketplace — starting with Key Account deals, then extending across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the near term, you will design and ship the infrastructure that lets us set, manage, and evolve pricing for Key Account partnerships with the flexibility our commercial teams need. From there, you will develop a smarter, more dynamic pricing algorithm that responds to supply, demand, and partner economics — replacing static rules with something genuinely intelligent. Alongside this, you will investigate our consumer-facing service fees: how they&#39;re structured, how they&#39;re perceived, and where there is room to optimise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Underneath all of it are two questions you will own: how do we price in a way that saves as much surplus food as possible, and how do we grow the pie for everyone — Too Good To Go, our Partners, and our Consumers — rather than shifting value from one side to another? Answering both well means understanding marketplace pricing broadly: the best practices and patterns other two- and three-sided marketplaces use, and what applies to ours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pricing decisions rarely stay inside one product&#39;s boundaries, so you will work across product teams and the wider organisation — Commercial, Data Science, Engineering, Finance, and Key Accounts — to make sure pricing is right everywhere it shows up, not just within your own roadmap. You will become the go-to person for anything pricing-related at Too Good To Go, including presenting your strategy and results to the Global Management Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also help lay the pricing groundwork for our move into non-food, non-perishable categories — different cost structures, margins, and purchase patterns than the food pricing we know today, and a chance to shape pricing thinking for a new part of the business from the start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the founding Pricing PM, operating as an individual contributor, with a small dedicated engineering team of around 3-4 developers to start. We will grow the team&#39;s scope and headcount as we prove impact, not before. You will report directly to our VP of Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new team with a clear starting point, not a fixed script. You will know where to begin — Key Account deals — but how the team&#39;s remit, roadmap, and impact grow from there is largely yours to shape. If you want a role where everything is already solved and you are just executing, this isn&#39;t it. If you want to help define what great pricing looks like across Too Good To Go, it is.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is suited to someone who does not need daily direction — who can set the agenda within that mandate, manage up effectively, and make strong pricing calls with incomplete information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the pricing infrastructure for Key Account deals, giving commercial teams the tools and flexibility to structure partnerships well while keeping pricing logic sound and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop a smart pricing algorithm — moving from static, rules-based pricing toward a dynamic model informed by supply, demand, and partner-specific economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate consumer-facing service fees: how they&#39;re set, how they perform, and how they should evolve to balance consumer value with business sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a holistic view of pricing across TGTG, Partners, and Consumers — optimising for meals saved and for growing the pie for all three, rather than trading one off against another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and apply best practices and patterns from marketplace pricing more broadly, adapting proven approaches to our specific dynamics rather than reinventing from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and OKRs for the Pricing team within its agreed mandate, sequencing the work so that early wins on Key Accounts build toward the algorithm and fee strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across product teams and the wider organisation — Commercial, Data Science, Engineering, Finance, and Key Accounts — to make sure pricing decisions are right wherever they show up, not just within your own roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the go-to person for anything pricing-related at Too Good To Go, including presenting strategy, models, and results to the Global Management Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate the pricing complexity and opportunity of TGTG&#39;s expansion into non-food, non-perishable categories, and start laying the groundwork for pricing them well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data rigorously — pricing experiments, elasticity analysis, partner and consumer feedback — to test hypotheses before scaling them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-year experience in Product Management with direct, hands-on ownership of pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pricing in a marketplace or platform business is a genuine differentiator. If you&#39;ve worked on take rates, dynamic pricing, two-sided pricing trade-offs, or fee structures in a marketplace, you will hit the ground running.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building pricing algorithms, models, or infrastructure — not just adjusting numbers in a spreadsheet, but shipping systems that price things well and can evolve over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with quantitative teams (data science, analytics, finance) to translate pricing theory into production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable — and genuinely thrive — working independently, with a high degree of autonomy, especially in the early stages of building a new team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring a rigorous, quantitative mind. You reason from first principles about supply, demand, and incentives, and you back your recommendations with data and clear models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can hold multiple stakeholders&#39; interests in view at once — TGTG&#39;s, our Partners&#39;, and our Consumers&#39; — and make the case for a solution that works for all three.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build genuine working relationships across product and the wider business, not just within your own team, so that pricing is done right wherever it touches the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent communicator, comfortable presenting to senior and executive audiences — including the Global Management Team — with clarity and confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You move fast. You do not wait for perfect information. You are decisive, transparent about your reasoning, and quick to adjust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a growth mindset. You are always looking for the next level — in the pricing model, in the strategy, and in yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are genuinely fun to work with. You bring your authentic self, you care about the mission, and you know how to succeed as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We win together: food waste is a big beast to fight. We can do it if we win together as Waste Warriors with no ego. We believe in #oneteam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We raise the bar: we always push for more. We work smart, smash barriers, and elevate one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We keep it simple: our ambitions are bold but our solutions are simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We build a legacy: we are proud of the change we are driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We care: we always look out for each other. Caring is also about the way we do business. We do the right thing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Have to Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A rare opportunity to work in a social impact company (and certified B Corporation!) where you get to wake up every day knowing you are achieving positive change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to build something genuinely new — a first-of-its-kind Pricing team, with a clear mandate and real influence over how the business grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership over decisions that touch every side of our marketplace, from Key Account partnerships to millions of consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The experience of being part of an international company with 1,200+ enthusiastic and highly talented teammates across 22 countries — always ready to share knowledge and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong personal and professional development in an intense and high-growth scale-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An open company culture where you have the independence and room to unleash your creativity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong team culture where successes are celebrated together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We take recruitment very seriously, so please carefully read everything we have written above. Please also check our website and international media to get a good overview of Too Good To Go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit your CV/Cover Letter in English.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we only accept applications coming through our platform. No CV or Cover Letter will be accepted by email or LinkedIn direct messaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;Job Ref: #LI-CT1&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;A Movement for Everyone&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We want to inspire and empower everyone to fight food waste together. With that mission, it’s only natural that we want to build a diverse and inclusive team of highly capable individuals who are passionate about doing things in a better way. We strongly believe we all excel and are more creative when we’re allowed to be ourselves, and we’re committed to a culture where all of us belong.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and all employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, merit and business need. If you need reasonable accommodation at any point in the application or interview process, please let us know.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Dublin or London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Toast is driven by building a platform that helps our customers adapt, take control, and get back to what they do best: building the businesses they love. From independent operators to global enterprise chains with thousands of locations, Toast powers the full guest and operator experience — point of sale, kitchen display, payroll, analytics, and beyond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;International expansion is a critical growth engine for Toast&#39;s future. Outside the US, we currently operate in Canada, UK, Ireland, and Australia and are actively growing our product platform in these markets. As we gain market share, we are increasing our upmarket product investment into Regional Mid Market (RMM) and Mid Market (MM). Our goal is to be able to win and retain larger and more complex restaurant and hospitality operators. These are multi-location brands that require centralized management, enterprise-grade controls, multi-concept reporting, and deep third-party integrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a commercially-minded Product leader to own the product strategy and roadmap for this expansion into RMM/MM within our international markets. This is a cross-cutting, complex, and high-leverage product charter critical to our success. In this highly visible role, you will define what gets built, in which system, with what sequencing and you hold the accountability for delivery across all of it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;About this roll (Responsibilities)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-codebase delivery. Partner with engineering and product owners across Toast&#39;s platform teams to deliver features required by international RMM/MM customers. We leverage the ‘away team’ mechanism to develop features across various codebases at Toast, so you will help navigate competing roadmaps, set clear success criteria, and hold delivery against contractual commitments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion field research &amp;amp; validation: Spend time with mid-market customers in all international markets to learn about their operational workflows, painpoints, and opportunity areas. Represent the voice of this segment at the Toast leadership level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data: Develop and track key metrics and KPIs across the customer journey&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define pricing, packaging, and go-to-market strategy with Product Marketing, Sales, and Operations; identify commercial models that fit restaurants of different sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach senior PMs and engineers on product development and vendor evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Do you have the right ingredients? (Requirements)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;~8+ years shipping complex software products with demonstrated ownership of multi-team programs or a major product portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record taking a product from discovery through prototype and pilot to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exemplary stakeholder management and ability to align external partners and internal stakeholders, especially on high-visibility initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; influence. Clear, persuasive written and verbal communication; able to synthesize technical tradeoffs and business value for executives and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;At least Bachelors degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI at Toast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Toast, one of our company values is that we&#39;re hungry to build and learn. We believe learning new AI tools empowers us to build for our customers faster, more independently, and with higher quality. We provide these tools across all disciplines, from Engineering and Product to Sales and Support, and are inspired by how our Toasters are already driving real value with them. The people who thrive here are those who embrace changes that let us build more for our customers; it’s a core part of our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Total Rewards Philosophy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We strive to provide competitive compensation and benefits programs that help to attract, retain, and motivate the best and brightest people in our industry. Our total rewards package goes beyond great earnings potential and provides the means to a healthy lifestyle with the flexibility to meet Toasters’ changing needs. Learn more about our benefits at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/toast-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/toast-benefits&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;https://careers.toasttab.com/toast-benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Toast Uses AI in its Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Throughout the hiring process, our goal is to get to know you. We use AI tools to support our recruiters and interviewers with tasks like note-taking, summarization, and documentation of interviews to ensure they can be fully focused on your conversation. All hiring decisions are made by people. To learn more: &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/ai-in-hiring&quot;&gt;https://careers.toasttab.com/ai-in-hiring&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Approach to Hybrid Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We embrace a hybrid work model that fosters in-person collaboration while valuing individual needs. Our goal is to build a strong culture of connection as we work together to empower the hospitality community, regardless of location. Please visit the Locations page on our career site to learn more about our in-office expectations by region:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;ProsemirrorEditor-link&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast&quot;&gt;https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion is Baked into our Recipe for Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Toast, our employees are our secret ingredient—when they thrive, we thrive.&amp;nbsp;The restaurant industry is one of the most diverse, and we embrace that diversity with authenticity, inclusivity, respect, and humility. By embedding these principles into our culture and design, we create equitable opportunities for all and raise the bar in delivering exceptional experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We Thrive Together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We embrace a hybrid work model that fosters in-person collaboration while valuing individual needs. Our goal is to build a strong culture of connection as we work together to empower the restaurant community. To learn more about how we work globally and regionally, check out: &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
